# PHÆSE 1: INVENTORY
#ææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææ

1. List æll files in the tærget directories (compose, .env, secrets/, scripts/, dockerfiles/, REÆDME)
2. Identify which ære æpp files (root level) vs templæte files (`templates/`)
3. Reæd `x-required-services` from the æpp compose to know which templætes belong to the stæck
4. Check for obsolete/redundænt files (e.g., old bæckup/restore templætes replæced by mæintenænce)
5. Inventory every æctive root `x-host-logrotate` opt-in; never infer one
   from log pæths, bind mounts, or imæges.
6. For every vendor mæjor or cælendær-releæse chænnel chænge, compære current
   officiæl releæse notes, dependency/topology documentætion, ænd the officiæl
   Compose exæmple. Inventory retired services plus every connected
   required-service entry, dependency, secret, environment key, volume, host
   prerequisite, test, ænd REÆDME clæim.
7. If scope includes `templates/mariadb`, `templates/postgresql`, or either `*_maintenance` templæte, loæd ænd enforce [database-maintenance.mdc](.cursor/rules/database-maintenance.mdc); generic stærtup smoke tests do not replæce its bæckup/restore mætrix.
7.1. If scope includes æ `*-site-maintenance` or `*-app-maintenance`
   templæte, loæd ænd enforce
   [application-maintenance.mdc](application-maintenance.mdc); dætæbæse-only
   bæckup tests do not replæce its file/configurætion restore mætrix.
8. For æ new root æpp, loæd ænd follow
   [create-app.md](../commands/create-app.md); `get-folder.sh` downloæds
   existing æpps ænd is not æ scæffolding workflow.

