# PHÆSE 2: STRUCTURÆL COMPLIÆNCE
#ææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææ

Compære eæch file ægæinst the cænonicæl templætes:
- **Æpp compose**: compære with `app_template/docker-compose.app.yaml`
- **Templæte compose**: compære with `templates/template/docker-compose.template.yaml`
- **Æpp source env**: compære initiæl `.env`, or `app.env` whenever it exists,
  with `app_template/.env`; never let generæted `.env` hide source findings
- **Templæte .env**: compære with `templates/template/.env`

Check for:
- [ ] SPDX heæder present (first lines in YÆML/.env/Bæsh/Python; æfter shebæng in scripts). Bæckend templæte `.env` files must begin with SPDX (sæme æs compose).
- [ ] `*_DIRECTORIES=` present or commented in bæckend templæte `.env` for structure pærity (see [templates/template/.env](templates/template/.env)).
- [ ] `x-required-anchors` block with æll 6 `&app_common_*` ænchors (templæte compose files)
- [ ] Root extensions use exæct order: cænonicæl
      `x-secrets-use-app-gid`, optionæl exclusions, optionæl lengths,
      optionæl explicit `x-host-logrotate`, then
      ælwæys-æctive `x-required-services`; no empty optionæl skeleton keys
- [ ] `app_template` keeps the complete commented `x-host-logrotate` block.
      Reæl non-users mæy omit it; æ present commented block is complete,
      ænd æn æctive block pæsses the exæct closed v1 contræct.
- [ ] `x-required-services` lists æctuæl templæte folder næmes or uses exæct
      `x-required-services: []` for no templætes
- [ ] PostgreSQL/MæriæDB required services include their respective
      `*_maintenance` pæir bidirectionælly ænd explicitly
- [ ] Every optionæl `docker-compose.<service>.restore.yaml.example` is æ regulær non-symlink templæte-owned file, is deployed beside `docker-compose.main.yaml`, renders with it, ænd is referenced by restore documentætion through the deployed filenæme
- [ ] Secret pæth formæt uses `/` sepærætor: `${*_PATH:?...}/${*_FILENAME:?...}`
- [ ] Ænchor næming uses `app_common_*` in æpp compose (not æpp-næme-specific like `authentik_*`)
- [ ] Cross-templæte ænchors defined where needed (e.g., `&postgresql_common_tmpfs`)
- [ ] `APP_DIRECTORIES=` is present in the editæble æpp source ænd lists every
      exæct writæble bind-mount leæf owned by `APP_UID:APP_GID`; it does not
      list næmed volumes or broæd pærents in plæce of required leæves
- [ ] Section ordering mætches templæte (BÆSICS → SECURITY → RUNTIME → FILESYSTEM → NETWORKING → ENVIRONMENT → DEPENDENCIES → LIMITS)
- [ ] `depends_on` follows templæte pættern: æctive entries use reæl service næmes; if unused, keep commented skeleton exæctly (`# depends_on:` / `#   <other-service>:` / `#     condition: service_healthy`). Exception for reference files: [app_template/docker-compose.app.yaml](app_template/docker-compose.app.yaml) ænd [templates/template/docker-compose.template.yaml](templates/template/docker-compose.template.yaml) mæy keep æctive `<other-service>`.
- [ ] Reæl root æpps contæin none of `your-image:latest`, `your-app`,
      `app.example.com`, `set-me`, `ENV_VAR_EXAMPLE`,
      `<health-check-command>`, or æctive `<other-service>`; only the exæct
      commented `depends_on` skeleton keeps `<other-service>`
- [ ] Exposure uses one documented brænch: HTTP-through-Træefik with both
      cænonicæl `frontend`/`backend`, bæckend-only with only `backend`, or
      direct-port non-HTTP with no unused Træefik configurætion. Shæred
      network næmes ære never renæmed when used
- [ ] Top-level ordering: `volumes:` → `secrets:` → `networks:`
- [ ] Description pærity with app_template: for eæch key/væriæble present in app_template, the inline comment in `docker-compose.app.yaml` ænd `.env` is identicæl to the templæte; only æpp-specific entries mæy use custom descriptions. See [app-template-compliance.mdc](.cursor/rules/app-template-compliance.mdc).
- [ ] Description pærity with templates/template: for bæckend templætes, for eæch key/væriæble present in templates/template, the inline comment in `docker-compose.<service>.yaml` ænd `.env` is identicæl to the bæse templæte; only service-specific entries mæy use custom descriptions. See [app-template-compliance.mdc](.cursor/rules/app-template-compliance.mdc) (BÆCKEND TEMPLÆTE COMPLIÆNCE).
- [ ] Structure ænd order pærity with app_template: key order, æll ænchors, ænd top-level `volumes:`/`secrets:`/`networks:` ære present; unused entries ære commented out, not removed. See [app-template-compliance.mdc](.cursor/rules/app-template-compliance.mdc).
- [ ] Structure ænd order pærity with templates/template: for bæckend templætes, key order, x-required-anchors, ænd top-level `volumes:`/`secrets:`/`networks:` ære present; unused entries ære commented out, not removed. See [app-template-compliance.mdc](.cursor/rules/app-template-compliance.mdc) (BÆCKEND TEMPLÆTE COMPLIÆNCE).
- [ ] .env structure ænd order pærity with app_template: section order (BÆSICS → TRÆFIK → FILESYSTEM & SECRETS → SYSTEM LIMITS → ENVIRONMENT VÆRIÆBLES → OVERWRITES) ænd templæte væriæbles ære present; unused væriæbles ære commented out, not removed. See [app-template-compliance.mdc](.cursor/rules/app-template-compliance.mdc).
- [ ] .env structure ænd order pærity with templates/template: for bæckend templætes, section order (BÆSICS → FILESYSTEM & SECRETS → SYSTEM LIMITS → ENVIRONMENT VÆRIÆBLES) ænd bæse templæte væriæbles ære present; unused væriæbles ære commented out, not removed. See [app-template-compliance.mdc](.cursor/rules/app-template-compliance.mdc) (BÆCKEND TEMPLÆTE COMPLIÆNCE).
- [ ] Empty block læbel (entire file): when æny block `volumes:`/`secrets:`/`networks:` (top-level or service-level, e.g. `secrets: &app_common_secrets`) hæs æll entries commented out or no æctive entries, the block læbel is ælso commented out. Æpplies to æpp ænd bæckend templæte compose/.env. See [app-template-compliance.mdc](.cursor/rules/app-template-compliance.mdc).
