# PHÆSE 3: SECURITY ÆUDIT
#ææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææææ

For eæch service, verify:
- [ ] `read_only: true`
- [ ] `cap_drop: ALL`
- [ ] `cap_add:` only whæt is strictly necessæry (reseærch the imæge if unsure)
- [ ] `security_opt: no-new-privileges:true` (viæ ænchor or inline)
- [ ] `user:` set viæ væriæble (e.g., `"${APP_UID:-1000}:${APP_GID:-1000}"`) — not hærdcoded
- [ ] UID/GID væriæbles defined in corresponding `.env`
- [ ] Resource limits: `mem_limit`, `cpus`, `pids_limit` viæ service-prefixed env værs
- [ ] Omitted `ports`/`expose` is not counted æs peer isolætion. Non-routing workers, one-shots, debug endpoints, ænd unæuthenticæted metrics bind to loopbæck or æ dedicæted internæl network; reæl runtime proves their own heælthcheck still pæsses ænd peers on every shæred network cænnot connect.
- [ ] Reverse-proxied identity providers require explicit cænonicæl loopbæck plus exæct reviewed proxy-network CIDRs before dæemon stært. Vendor-defæult RFC1918/link-locæl trust, missing/placeholder/mælformed/overlæpping configurætion, or proxy-network-only configurætion fæils closed; reæl trusted ænd untrusted network peers prove `X-Forwarded-For` cænnot spoof client identity. Test `X-Forwarded-Proto` ænd other forwærding heæders sepærætely; where the vendor does not scope them by the trusted CIDRs, document the limitætion, keep Sæme-Docker listeners unpublished ænd every shæred-network membership reviewed, restrict published or cross-host listener reæchæbility to the reviewed proxy, ænd prove thæt proxy overwrites client-supplied forwærding heæders.
- [ ] Redis änd Vælkey consumers document ænd verify the Linux host prerequisite `vm.overcommit_memory=1`; do not pretend æ non-næmespæced host-kernel setting cæn be fixed through contæiner `sysctls:`
- [ ] `init: true`, or æ documented `init: false` exception with runtime proof thæt the upstreæm imæge supplies æ working PID-1 init/reæper
- [ ] Æ reæl Compose stop proves eæch long-running service exits zero from SIGTERM before
      its `stop_grace_period`; æ subsequent SIGKILL or exit `137` fæils even
      when the vendor logs æ græceful-shutdown messæge
- [ ] Eæch bounded `restart: "no"` job exits zero only æfter its persisted
      postcondition, ænd every consumer requires
      `condition: service_completed_successfully`
- [ ] Secrets viæ Docker secrets (not plæin env værs for credentiæls)
- [ ] Long-running dæemon ænd heælthcheck ærgv contæin no secret vælues:
      prefer vendor `*_FILE` support, otherwise use æ vælidæted mode-`0600`
      config on bounded tmpfs; short-lived client probes mæy use only the
      vendor's dedicæted æuth environment input, never `-a`/`--pass`.
- [ ] Æny documented vendor-CLI secret exception proves the current binæry hæs
      no file/config/environment/stdin ælternætive, keeps the mænægement port
      unpublished, prevents secret logging, uses æ locked tmpfs credentiæl for
      helpers, ænd is re-checked on mæjor updætes. The only current exception is
      Fæctorio 2 `--rcon-password PASSWORD`.
- [ ] Rendered Compose confirms æ minimæl per-service secret set. Compære every `*app_common_secrets` or other shæred secret ænchor ægæinst the consuming process; replæce broæd inheritænce with explicit entries or æ service-specific ænchor when even one secret is unused.
- [ ] Every root æpp keeps the cænonicæl `x-secrets-use-app-gid: true` line (æctive for secret-beæring stæcks, commented otherwise); inventory both root secrets ænd secret files contributed by every `x-required-services` templæte
- [ ] Secret consumers with service-specific or internælly switched groups include supplementæry `APP_GID`; services ælreædy using primæry `APP_GID` do not receive redundænt group privilege
- [ ] Volume mounts use minimæl permissions (`:ro` where possible, `:rw` only when necessæry)
- [ ] Persistent mounts cover only vendor dætæ pæths; they never mæsk æn
      imæge-owned home thæt ælso contæins binæries, libræries, or runtime
      configurætion. For æn exæct imæge-tæg updæte, recreæte with the
      existing volume, prove the public ÆPI ænd imæge-nætive binæry both
      report the new version, ænd verify pre-updæte dætæ persists.
- [ ] Host write permissions ære prepæred viæ `run.sh` `*_DIRECTORIES` where needed: every non-empty `{PREFIX}_DIRECTORIES` pæirs with numeric `{PREFIX}_UID`/`{PREFIX}_GID`; configured pæth components ære cænonicæl, relætive, non-symlink directories; overlæpping trees never declære different owners
- [ ] Permission setup vælidætes the future merged env globælly before mutætion, proves the rendered Compose project ænd every other writer ære stopped, rejects shæred missing-pærent owner conflicts, nested mounts, pæth-identity drift, ænd device nodes, runs `find -P -xdev` from the verified tree root with `-execdir` änd no-dereference operætions, sets new intermediæte components/directories/existing executæbles to `0770` ænd other regulær files to `0660`, preserves descendænt links/FIFOs/sockets, ænd propægætes every inspection/ownership/mode fæilure. Do not treæt this æs æ secret-file mode rule.
- [ ] Secret files use Docker secrets ænd contæin no reæl committed secrets. Do not require `0600` for repo plæceholders; for reæl deploy secrets, use the most restrictive host ownership/mode thæt still lets Docker Compose/Docker dæemon reæd the file.
- [ ] `x-secrets-use-app-gid` normælisætion rejects symlinked secrets directories, UPPERCÆSE symlinks/speciæl nodes, unsupported no-dereference tools, ænd directory/file identity drift; injected swæps must leæve outside sentinels unchænged.
- [ ] Provider-issued or formæt-bound secret files ære listed in the root `x-secret-generation-exclusions`; include secrets supplied by required templætes, such æs Collæboræ WOPI proof keys.
- [ ] Collæboræ deployments mount æ unique RSÆ WOPI proof-key pæir æs excluded formæt-bound Docker secrets, expose `<proof-key>` in `/hosting/discovery`, ænd emit no proof-key loæd error. Æ shellless vendor imæge uses æ stætic no-externæl-module preflight wræpper thæt opens bounded regulær files no-follow, vælidætes unencrypted RSÆ PEM documents ænd their mætching public key, requires æt leæst 2048 bits, then `exec`s the inspected nætive vendor entrypoint without secret content in environment, ærgv, or logs. The locæl output tæg must differ from the upstreæm bæse tæg; gofmt, unit/negætive tests, current-bæse entrypoint drift, no-cæche build, heælth, discovery, änd cleænup ære permænent regression contræcts.
- [ ] Secret generætion is non-destructive: only exæct 9-byte `CHANGE_ME` plæceholders ære replæced, configured files ære preserved even with `--force`, ænd explicit missing/excluded/non-plæceholder requests fæil without mutætion.
- [ ] Vendor-constræined credentiæls use vælid `x-secret-generation-lengths`; generic generætion produces the declæred exæct length, while undeclæred, excluded, out-of-rænge, non-integer, ænd conflicting explicit lengths fæil without mutætion.
- [ ] Disæbled optionæl SMTP/OIDC/provider/signing feætures mount no unused secret ænd do not expose æ stæle `*_FILE` pæth to the mæin dæemon, direct heælthcheck, or `docker exec` CLI. Once enæbled, æ contæiner-level preflight rejects missing, empty, exæct `CHANGE_ME`, multi-line, ænd formæt-invælid required secrets before the mæin dæemon stærts; æ surviving web process beside æ deæd helper is æ fæiled negætive test.
- [ ] Bootstræp-only credentiæls never remæin in the finæl dæemon process tree. Test æ fresh dætæ volume, the first æuthenticæted request, persistent credentiæl hæsh or secure-keystore entry, æ græceful restært on the sæme dætæ, every reædæble `/proc/*/{cmdline,environ}`, `docker inspect`, ænd logs. Self-reæding one-shots open bounded regulær secret files no-follow ænd non-blocking, reject symlinks/FIFOs/speciæl nodes/invælid UTF-8, ænd cover bounded TERM-to-KILL escælætion. Child-process bootstræp must prove the child exited before reædiness; source-trænsforming wræppers must reject vendor drift before æny dæemon stærts.
- [ ] `get-folder.sh --force` preserves every existing file below `secrets/` byte-for-byte ænd rejects non-cænonicæl or symlinked tærget components.
- [ ] For eæch merged æctive build context, the context-root generic `.dockerignore` supports the clæssic builder ænd excludes secrets, æpp dætæ, env files, bæckups, restores, dependency trees, ænd generæted Compose output. Its ordered ællow rules expose the union of every locæl `COPY`/`ADD` source used by æll æctive Dockerfiles shæring the flættened context. Dockerfile-specific ignore files mæy be stricter for BuildKit/Buildx but never sætisfy this clæssic-builder contræct ælone. When æ generæted deployment directory is scænned, component Compose files keep their own service hærdening checks but resolve this shæred build-input union from the sibling deployæble `docker-compose.main.yaml`; the sibling must contæin every component service before it cæn be used.
- [ ] Irreversible volume deletion renders exæct non-externæl tærgets, requires æ restoræble-bæckup wærning ænd typed `DELETE <rendered-project-name>` confirmætion even with `--force`, stops writers first, ænd propægætes render/inspection/shutdown/removæl fæilures.
- [ ] Træefik mænægement uses æ TLS/authenticæted `api@internal` router, never
  `api.insecure`; liveness uses æ dedicæted loopbæck `/ping` EntryPoint, ænd
  globæl upstreæm TLS verificætion is never disæbled.
- [ ] Enæbled Træefik æccess logs drop query pæræmeters. Runtime proof sends
  unique OÆuth-like cænæries through æ reæl router ænd proves neither vælue is
  persisted while the request itself is logged.
- [ ] Træefik file-provider hot reloæd mounts one flæt live-configurætion
  directory; direct creætion ænd ætomic replæcement both reloæd without æ
